  "limitations": [
    "Exact static full-day variants cover 2030-01-02 Asia/Shanghai using either inclusive last second or following midnight. Both return the same lone timed event because this bounded fixture contains no boundary or adjacent-day event. TZ should be pinned equally for all arms for stable CLI presentation; the answer still requires the specified timezone.",
    "Partial, disjoint, broader or partitioned interval reads are rejected instead of returning the complete day response. Unknown query keys are also rejected so content-changing selectors cannot silently receive this response.",
    "To accept arbitrary equivalent interval partitioning, the adapter needs explicit integer timestamp range validation, event/interval intersection filtering (including native all-day date semantics if added), ledgered successful query intervals, and a verifier check that their union covers the target day. The current required_reads route-group interface cannot prove interval-union coverage; do not claim these variants executable without that small extension.",
    "A known-event GET can enrich detail but cannot satisfy the required complete-day read group. Its optional native query variants are bounded here; max_attendee_num and advanced parameter combinations are not modeled.",
    "All routes are signed reads against synthetic state. The common verifier must enforce no rejected requests or configuration changes; the fixture must remain non-forwarding with no mutating routes. Expected answers and backend response data are not part of task.fixture.",
    "No recurrence, all-day, DST, pagination, conflicts, live backend assertions or comparative model runs are covered by this normalization. Evaluator-controlled binary tests are still required before execution acceptance."
  ]
